---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Proportion" currentPath="/plates/proportion">
  <div class="breadcrumb">
    <a href="/">Entry</a> / <a href="/plates">Plates</a> / Proportion
  </div>

  <article class="principle-document">
    <header class="principle-header">
      <div class="principle-meta">
        <span class="principle-number">E02-P05</span>
        <span class="edition">Edition 02</span>
        <span class="see-also">See also: <a href="/texts/human-patterns">T05 Human Patterns</a></span>
      </div>
      <h1>Proportion creates harmony</h1>
      <p class="abstract">Relationships between sizes matter more than absolute measurements.</p>
    </header>

    <section class="principle-content">
      <h2>Statement</h2>
      <p>The mind judges elements relationally.</p>
      <p>A heading is not "24 pixels"—it is 1.5× the body text.</p>

      <h2>Context</h2>
      <p>
        Proportion is the mathematics of visual harmony. When elements relate to each other through consistent ratios—when a heading is precisely twice the size of body text, when margins follow a geometric sequence, when the golden ratio governs spatial division—the composition feels resolved. This is not mysticism. It is pattern recognition operating at a neurological level.
      </p>
      <p>
        Poor proportion produces visual discord. Elements sized arbitrarily, with no mathematical relationship between them. A heading 23 pixels, body text 16 pixels, a subhead 19 pixels. The ratios are irrational. The eye registers the lack of system and searches for one that isn't there.
      </p>

      <h2>Application</h2>
      <p>
        Proportion operates through ratios: typographic scales (1:1.2, 1:1.414, 1:1.618), spacing systems (4px, 8px, 16px, 32px), grid divisions (halves, thirds, golden sections). The specific ratio matters less than its consistency. Once established, it should govern all spatial and scalar decisions.
      </p>
      <p>
        In practice: Typography should follow a modular scale. Spacing should increment geometrically, not arbitrarily. Layout grids should divide space mathematically. When proportion is systematic, every measurement feels inevitable rather than accidental.
      </p>

      <h2>Citation</h2>
      <p class="citation-text">
        This principle may be cited as: <strong>E02-P05 (Proportion)</strong>. For mathematical foundations, see <a href="/texts/human-patterns">T05 Human Patterns</a>.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .breadcrumb {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--color-reading-ink);
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
  }

  .breadcrumb a {
    color: var(--color-reading-ink);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  .breadcrumb a:hover {
    color: var(--color-ink);
  }

  .principle-document {
    max-width: 700px;
  }

  .principle-header {
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
    padding-bottom: 2rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  .principle-meta {
    display: flex;
    gap: 1.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    font-family: var(--font-ui);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--color-muted);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }

  .principle-meta .see-also {
    font-style: italic;
    text-transform: none;
  }

  .principle-meta .see-also a {
    color: var(--color-ink);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  .principle-header h1 {
    font-size: 2.25rem;
    font-weight: 400;
    line-height: 1.2;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .abstract {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--color-reading-ink);
    font-style: italic;
  }

  .principle-content h2 {
    font-size: 1.3rem;
    font-weight: 400;
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .principle-content p {
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    line-height: 1.8;
  }

  .citation-text {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    color: var(--color-reading-ink);
    font-style: italic;
  }

  .citation-text strong {
    color: var(--color-ink);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-style: normal;
  }

  .citation-text a {
    color: var(--color-ink);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }
</style>
